CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty-pack decltype resolves: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A variadic forwarding helper whose trailing-return decltype contains a pack
expansion f(a...), deduced with an EMPTY pack, collapses to f() and resolves.
An empty deduced parameter pack (recorded nowhere by deduction because the
argument list is exhausted before the pack) is now recorded with size 0, so the
trailing-return pack expansion collapses to zero arguments.  Applies to both the
plain and forwarding-cast forms.  N5008 [temp.variadic]/5,7,
[temp.arg.explicit]/4.
